  "title": "# Build: shipped-features-r3 (ALL Opus, high thinking; this account has NO Fable) **Name:** Shipped…",
  "asked": "# Build: shipped-features-r3 (ALL Opus, high thinking; this account has NO Fable) **Name:** Shipped features · **Category:** Plugin ## Continue, don't restart Branch base: `claude/shipped-features-r2` (draft PR #350). Read `_claude/builds/progress/shipped-features.md` (HANDOFF) and the PR body. Done: s1 feature-ledger@1, s2 deploy-log@1. The previous session stopped at s3/s4 marked 'Blocked on Fable'. Push your work to `claude/shipped-features-r2` so it stays PR #350 (or open a new PR and close #350 as superseded, linking it). ## Brett's override (verbatim intent, Nov 4) Do s3 (conformance check + fixture `framework/spec/fixtures/feature-ledger.json`) and s4 (build hook contract) **on Opus**. Mark both 'Opus, needs Fable review' in the progress file and the PR. A pending item 'Fable review: Shipped features build hook contract' already exists for later. Do NOT stop for Fable anywhere in this build. ## NEW (Brett, voice, Nov 4): AI or plain feature splitting, as a setting \"Put a setting in the plugin to make it AI or plain, and every time it does the plain, add a task to a new plan in Plan Studio.\" - Setting **Feature splitting: Plain (default) / AI** in the plugin's settings (framework settings interface), also per run in the importer CLI/API (`--split plain|ai`). - **Plain** (zero tokens): one feature per PR-body bullet / build step, junk filtered (test lines, file lists, 'Generated with', checklists of commands), names trimmed to one line, type guessed by keywords (fix/UI/new/perf/docs/infra). - **AI**: the clean split with proof and the linked verbatim prompt (as in the spec). It runs on the server, so it uses the active Claude account. Show an estimated cost before an AI run and ask to confirm. - **Every Plain run adds a task to a Plan Studio plan named 'Feature list: AI cleanup'** (create it once if missing, category Feature): one checklist item per plain-split PR/build ('AI-split PR #332 Maintenance plugin (6 plain features)'), with a link to the rows. No duplicates on re-runs. Ticking/running AI cleanup on those items re-splits them with AI and ticks the item. A 'Run AI cleanup on N waiting' button in the plugin. - Rows show a small 'plain' / 'AI' chip, and a filter for it. - Default for the first backfill: **Plain**. ## The rest of the spec (unchanged) Everything in `/root/axf-builds/shipped-features-r2/.brief.md` (incl. Addenda 4-5: planned features show up instantly with statuses + Hide completed/pending; changes show up as edits) and `/root/axf-builds/shipped-features/.brief.md` (SQLite DB on the data volume, AmberX-AXF + axHub history back to first commit, deploy log writers, 3-level grid with View by PR/Plugin/App/Feature type/Build/Day/Repo/Flat, 'What Brett said' block, Live/Merged badges, API/MCP/CLI + voice). Never commit the ~300 unrelated worktree files. ## Rules Resumable steps (tick + HANDOFF + commit + push after every step). Book to a free named agent. Docs/README.md, tests, phone + desktop UI Review shots (non-blocking). PR **through the merge queue only**. Report in _claude/builds/reports/. Commits clean. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never lau…",
